    "note": "Introduced text as filed; Senate passage vote recorded, so later amendments are not in the text read. Struck: 'buy bulletproof vests'. Gun content is thin: the only change is how sale proceeds of forfeited weapons are used; the weapon-seizure and auction rules already in the section are not changed."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Miss. Code § 97-37-3(2)(b)): A weapon so forfeited to a law enforcement agency may be sold at auction as provided by Sections 19-3-85 and 21-39-21 to a federally-licensed firearms dealer, with the proceeds from such sale at auction to be used to purchase equipment for the seizing law enforcement agency."
